  "headline": "Iran opens the door to talks and crude falls 7% \u2014 while technology slides again into the midterms",
  "standfirst": "WTI fell 7.36% to $96.46 and Brent 7.63% after Iran said its supreme leader had authorised peace talks and offered to reopen Hormuz under conditions. The Nasdaq fell 1.07% and the S&P 0.51% as chip and hardware stocks kept falling, while the Dow rose 0.41% and most stocks gained. The ISM manufacturing index rose to 55.5. After the close Palantir reported revenue of $2.313bn, up 96%, well above its guide, and still traded lower. The book is flat; Q4 is -7.54 realised, heat 0R.",
